intonation: keep the exclamation over the sentence-final stamp

assign_major_phr_features in upper form, standing in for the lifted
rule: after the current-phrase values are in, an exclamation the
dispatch matched gets its pitch values back over the declarative
stamp. A frame local records the match because the current-phrase
rules move the scan a second mark test would read. Mid-sentence the
stamp never lands, so only final marks change. Battery and ear hold it.
diff --git a/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.up b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.up
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6482a31
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.up
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# assign_major_phr_features with the exclamation kept.
+#
+# The lifted rule calls exclam_phrase for a phrase ending in `!' and then
+# lets assign_sent_final_features stamp the declarative values over what it
+# set, so a final hey! reads flat where ETI shouts it. Mid-sentence the
+# stamp never lands and the exclamation stands, which is why only the final
+# mark goes missing.
+#
+# This records whether the exclamation matched and, after the current-phrase
+# values are in, writes its values back over the stamped ones. The test the
+# dispatcher ran is not run again: assign_currPhr_vals moves the scan, so a
+# second test would read the wrong place. A frame local carries the answer
+# across the calls instead.
+rule assign_major_phr_features takes 3
+  instead
+  local exhit bytes 4
+  set exhit to 0
+  call ZZget_parm_ptr2 arg 2 arg 1 arg 1 arg 2
+  call ZZfence_null
+  call ZZstarttest1
+  call period_phrase arg 1 arg 2
+  if answer is 0
+    go to tail
+  end
+  call ZZstarttest3
+  call comma_phrase
+  if answer is 0
+    go to tail
+  end
+  call ZZstarttest4
+  call question_phrase arg 1 arg 2
+  if answer is 0
+    go to tail
+  end
+  call ZZstarttest5
+  call exclam_phrase arg 1
+  if answer is 0
+    set exhit to 1
+    go to tail
+  end
+  call ZZstarttest2
+  call semicolon_phrase
+  place tail
+  call ZZstarttest6
+  call assign_sent_final_features
+  call ZZstarttest7
+  call assign_currPhr_vals arg 2
+  call ZZstarttest8
+  call assign_phr_final_anno_features
+  if exhit is 0
+    go to noex
+  end
+  set global half 2386 to global half 2116
+  set global half 2040 to global half 2048
+  place noex
+  and 0 into global half 1514
+  match
+end
